<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"></head><body>
<table border="1"><thead><tr><th>Requirement Name</th><th>ID</th><th>Text</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>REQ_BOX_SERIALIZATION</td><td>REQ-BOX-001</td><td>BoxRecord shall round-trip losslessly through toMap() and fromMap(),  preserving id, name, description (including null), fragile, and createdAt.  toExportMap() shall include at minimum id, name, and createdAt keys.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_ITEM_SERIALIZATION</td><td>REQ-ITEM-001</td><td>ItemRecord shall round-trip losslessly through toMap() and fromMap(),  preserving id, name, photoPath (including null), boxId, and createdAt.  toExportMap() shall omit photoPath and include the labels list.  Unknown label strings encountered in fromMap() shall be silently dropped  without throwing. Empty labels lists shall survive the round-trip.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_DB_BOX_CRUD</td><td>REQ-DB-001</td><td>DatabaseService shall support inserting a Box, returning all Boxes sorted  ascending by createdAt, upserting on duplicate id, updating mutable fields,  and deleting a Box by id. Deleting a Box shall cascade-delete all Items  whose boxId matches. All operations shall be idempotent with respect to  the backing store.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_DB_ITEM_CRUD</td><td>REQ-DB-002</td><td>DatabaseService shall support inserting an Item, returning Items for a  specific boxId (sorted ascending by createdAt, filtered to that box only),  returning all Items across all boxes, updating mutable Item fields,  deleting an Item by id, returning the count of Items for a given boxId,  and clearing all boxes and items in a single operation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_DB_SEARCH</td><td>REQ-DB-003</td><td>DatabaseService.searchItems() shall return an empty list for queries  shorter than 3 characters. For qualifying queries it shall perform a  case-insensitive substring match on Item.name, return each matching  Item paired with its parent Box, sort results alphabetically by item  name, and return an empty list when no items match.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_IO_EXPORT_PAYLOAD</td><td>REQ-IO-001</td><td>ImportExportService.buildExportPayload() shall produce a Map containing  app == "Bokses", version == "1.1", an exportedAt ISO-8601 timestamp,  and boxes and items arrays derived from DatabaseService. The payload  shall serialise to valid JSON via jsonEncode() without throwing.  An empty database shall produce empty arrays for boxes and items.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_IO_IMPORT</td><td>REQ-IO-002</td><td>ImportExportService.processImportJson() shall reject input that does not  begin with "{" (e.g. HTML) with a message containing "Invalid file".  It shall reject payloads where app != "Bokses" with a message containing  "Invalid Bokses". Valid payloads shall upsert all boxes and items via  DatabaseService. An item payload containing a photoData field shall  have its photoPath reconstructed as a data:image/jpeg;base64,&lt;data&gt; URI.  Empty boxes/items arrays shall be accepted without error.  The function shall return a human-readable result message reporting counts.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_BOX_NAME_VALIDATION</td><td>REQ-UI-001</td><td>The New Box and Edit Box forms shall reject an empty name with the  message "Name required". A whitespace-only name shall also be rejected  with "Name required". A name that matches an existing box name  (case-insensitive comparison) shall be rejected with  "A box with this name already exists". A valid, unique name shall be  accepted; an optional description field shall be saved when provided.  The same duplicate-name rule applies during edit, excluding the box  being edited from the uniqueness check.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_BOX_DELETE_UNDO</td><td>REQ-UI-002</td><td>Deleting a box from the HomeScreen shall immediately remove it from  the UI and the backing store. A snackbar with an "Undo" action shall  appear for at least 2500 ms. Tapping Undo shall restore the box and  all of its items to the backing store and redisplay the box in the UI.  If Undo is not tapped before the snackbar dismisses, the deletion is  permanent. Deleting a box shall also delete all child items.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_HOME_DISPLAY</td><td>REQ-UI-003</td><td>HomeScreen shall display a "Bokses" wordmark, box and item count chips  with correct singular/plural grammar (e.g. "1 box", "2 items"), and a  "New Box" FAB. When no boxes exist it shall show the empty state message  "No boxes yet!". When boxes exist the empty state shall be hidden.  Box cards shall show the box name and optional description.  Item count chips shall reflect the live count from DatabaseService.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SEARCH_UI</td><td>REQ-UI-004</td><td>Activating search on HomeScreen shall open an inline text field and  hide the New Box FAB. Entering fewer than 3 characters shall display  "Type at least 3 characters". A query with no matching items shall  display "No items found". A matching query shall display a result tile  showing the item name and the parent box name. A clear button shall  appear when the field is non-empty and shall reset the search state.  The back arrow shall exit search mode and restore the box list.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_ITEM_CRUD_UI</td><td>REQ-UI-005</td><td>BoxDetailScreen shall show an "Add Item" FAB and item list or the  "Box is empty!" empty state. Tapping "Add Item" shall open a form;  submitting an empty name shall show "Name required". A valid name shall  create an Item persisted to DatabaseService with the correct boxId.  The edit flow shall pre-populate the existing name; saving with an  empty name shall show "Name required". Deleting an item shall remove it  immediately, show an "Undo" snackbar, allow restoration via Undo,  and show the empty state when the last item is deleted.  Items without a photo shall show a placeholder icon.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_LABEL_UI</td><td>REQ-UI-006</td><td>Individual label badge widgets (FragileBadge, BatteryBadge, LiquidBadge)  shall render their respective label text ("FRAGILE", "BATTERY", "LIQUID").  LabelBadgesRow shall render no badges for an empty set, and exactly one  badge per label in the provided set. LabelPickerSheet shall show all  three label names, toggle selection state on tap, pre-check any  initially-selected labels, and return the selected list when "Done"  is tapped. The end-to-end label assignment flow shall show the badge  in the item list after saving.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_HOME_SORT</td><td>REQ-UI-007</td><td>Tapping a sort option in the HomeScreen summary bar shall immediately  re-sort the displayed box list without navigating away.  dateAsc shall order oldest boxes first; dateDesc newest first;  nameAsc alphabetically A→Z; nameDesc Z→A.  The active sort option shall be visually distinguished from inactive ones.  Sort state shall be preserved for the lifetime of the HomeScreen session.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_HOME_VIEW_TOGGLE</td><td>REQ-UI-008</td><td>Tapping the view mode toggle in the HomeScreen summary bar shall switch  between BoxCard grid layout and BoxListTile list layout.  Grid mode shall render dot-matrix BoxCards; list mode shall render  Slidable BoxListTiles. Both modes shall display box name, item count,  and label badges. The toggle control shall reflect the current mode.  Mode state shall be preserved for the lifetime of the HomeScreen session.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_LIST_TILE_SWIPE</td><td>REQ-UI-009</td><td>In list view mode, dragging a BoxListTile with a short swipe shall  reveal an Edit action button and a Delete action button via the Slidable  DrawerMotion. Tapping the revealed Edit action shall open the edit box  sheet pre-populated with the box's current name and description.  Tapping the revealed Delete action shall immediately remove the box,  show the Undo snackbar, and cascade-delete all child items — identical  in behaviour to the popup-menu delete path (REQ-UI-002).  A full-swipe dismiss shall also trigger the delete-with-undo flow.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_CLEAR_ALL_DIALOG</td><td>REQ-UI-010</td><td>Tapping "Clear All" from the HomeScreen overflow menu shall open an  AlertDialog requiring explicit confirmation before any data is deleted.  Tapping the cancel button shall dismiss the dialog and leave all boxes  and items intact. Tapping the confirm button shall call  DatabaseService.clearAll() and update HomeScreen to show the empty state.  The dialog shall not be dismissible by tapping outside its bounds.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_MOVE_ITEM_UI</td><td>REQ-UI-011</td><td>In BoxDetailScreen, swiping an item tile shall reveal a Move action  alongside the Edit and Delete actions. Tapping Move shall present a  popup listing all other boxes by name. Selecting a target box shall call  DatabaseService.updateItem() with the updated boxId, remove the item  from the current screen immediately, and reflect the updated item count  on HomeScreen when returning. If no other boxes exist, the Move action  shall be disabled or absent.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_PHOTO_UI</td><td>REQ-UI-012</td><td>The Add Item and Edit Item forms shall each contain a camera icon button.  Tapping the button shall invoke ImagePicker for the device camera.  If the picker returns a path, a thumbnail preview shall appear in the  form before the item is saved. Submitting the form shall persist the  returned path as ItemRecord.photoPath.  If ImagePicker returns null (user cancelled), the form state shall  remain unchanged. Items with a stored photoPath shall display the photo  image in the item tile; items without a photo shall display the  placeholder icon (covered by REQ-UI-005).</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_BOX_FRAGILE_TOGGLE</td><td>REQ-UI-013</td><td>The New Box and Edit Box forms shall contain a toggle labelled "Fragile"  corresponding to BoxRecord.fragile. The toggle shall default to off for  new boxes. In the Edit Box form the toggle shall be pre-set to the  box's current fragile value. Saving with the toggle on shall persist  BoxRecord.fragile = true via DatabaseService.insertBox() or updateBox().  Saving with the toggle off shall persist BoxRecord.fragile = false.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SETTINGS_PERSISTENCE</td><td>REQ-SETTINGS-001</td><td>SettingsService shall return correct hardcoded defaults for every key  when SharedPreferences has no stored value: isDarkMode=true,  themePreset=0, backgroundType=none, talkSilenceMs=1500,  talkReadBack=false, loadAllContent=true, autoBoksCameraEnabled=true,  backgroundBlur=10.0, backgroundColor=0xFF0C0C0E, autoBoksSuccessCount=0.  Every setter shall persist its value so the corresponding getter  returns the new value in the same session.  incrementAutoBoksSuccessCount() shall be additive across calls.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SETTINGS_SCREEN_DARK_MODE</td><td>REQ-SETTINGS-002</td><td>The SettingsScreen dark mode toggle shall write the new value to  SharedPreferences under the key "is_dark_mode" immediately when  toggled. The SettingsScreen shall render a "Dark Mode" labelled  control and a "Camera" toggle in the AutoBoks section.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SETTINGS_THEME_PRESETS</td><td>REQ-SETTINGS-003</td><td>The SettingsScreen Appearance section shall render all 8 colour preset  chips (BoksOtter through Robin). Tapping a preset chip shall immediately  call AppTheme.setPreset() with the corresponding index and persist the  selection via SettingsService.setThemePreset(). The active chip shall be  visually distinguished from inactive chips. After a ValueNotifier-driven  rebuild the correct chip shall remain selected.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SETTINGS_BACKGROUND</td><td>REQ-SETTINGS-004</td><td>The SettingsScreen Background section shall render controls for all four  AppBgType options (none, gradient, image, solid). Selecting "none" shall  persist AppBgType.none and hide any sub-controls. Selecting "gradient"  shall persist AppBgType.gradient with no additional input. Selecting  "image" shall show a blur sigma slider (range 0–20); dragging it shall  call SettingsService.setBackgroundBlur() and trigger  AppTheme.notifyBgChanged(). Selecting "solid" shall show a colour input.  Each selection shall persist the chosen AppBgType via  SettingsService.setBackgroundType().</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SETTINGS_CV_BUTTONS</td><td>REQ-SETTINGS-005</td><td>The SettingsScreen CV Model section shall show a download button when  CV is enabled and the model is not installed. Tapping the download button  shall begin the download and replace the button with a progress bar  filling 0.0→1.0 as ModelService.download() emits progress. A cancel  button shall be available during download; tapping it shall abort the  download and return to the not-installed state. Once installed, a delete  button shall replace the progress bar; tapping it shall call  ModelService.delete() and revert the section to the not-installed state.  When the CV toggle is disabled, neither button nor progress bar shall appear.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_NAVIGATION</td><td>REQ-NAV-001</td><td>Tapping a box card on HomeScreen shall navigate to BoxDetailScreen  showing that box's content. The back button on BoxDetailScreen shall  return to HomeScreen. Tapping a search result tile shall navigate to  the BoxDetailScreen for the item's parent box. The settings icon shall  open SettingsScreen. The back button from SettingsScreen shall return  to HomeScreen. The "About" overflow menu item shall open AboutScreen.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_VERSION_HISTORY_NAV</td><td>REQ-NAV-002</td><td>The App Info section of SettingsScreen shall display the current app  version string and a tappable element labelled "Version History".  Tapping it shall push VersionHistoryScreen onto the Navigator stack.  The back button from VersionHistoryScreen shall return to SettingsScreen.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_ITEM_COUNT_ACCURACY</td><td>REQ-E2E-001</td><td>The item count displayed on a box card or list tile on HomeScreen  shall reflect the live count in DatabaseService after returning from  BoxDetailScreen. Adding one item and navigating back shall show  "1 item". Adding three items to the same box shall show "3 items".</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_SHARED_WIDGETS</td><td>REQ-WIDGET-001</td><td>BoksCard shall render its child widget and fire its onTap callback  when tapped. BoksBadge shall render its label text. AboutScreen shall  display an "About" app bar title and the application name "Bokses"  in the body. VersionHistoryScreen shall display a "Version History"  app bar title and at least one version badge containing "v0.".</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_BOX_CARD_DOTS</td><td>REQ-WIDGET-002</td><td>The BoxCard dot-matrix shall render 15 slots. Filled slots (indices 0 to  itemCount − 1, capped at 14) shall be visually distinct from empty slots.  When itemCount is 0, all 15 slots shall appear empty. When itemCount  exceeds 14, slot 14 shall display a "+" overflow indicator instead of  a filled dot. The card border colour shall lerp from boksBlue (index 0)  to boksRed (last index in the sorted list) via the accentColor value.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_BOX_FRAGILE_DISPLAY</td><td>REQ-WIDGET-003</td><td>When BoxRecord.fragile is true, both BoxCard and BoxListTile shall  display a fragile indicator on the card or tile surface. When  BoxRecord.fragile is false, no fragile indicator shall appear.  The box-level fragile flag is distinct from the item-level  ItemLabel::fragile badge; both may appear simultaneously if the box  is fragile and also contains fragile-labelled items.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_AUTOBOKS_SESSION</td><td>REQ-AUTO-001</td><td>AutoBoksController shall enforce the AutoBoksState machine across its  full session lifecycle: idle → requestingPermissions → listening →  silenceCountdown → capturing → readingBack → listening. Transitions  shall be atomic; simultaneous snap-sound and camera capture shall fire  in the same async frame. A permission-denied result shall transition  to the error state and prevent the session from starting. Calling  stopSession() from listening or silenceCountdown shall return to idle.  Each successful capture shall increment SettingsService.autoBoksSuccessCount.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_AUTOBOKS_UI</td><td>REQ-AUTO-002</td><td>BoxDetailScreen shall display an AutoBoks activation button. Tapping it  shall call AutoBoksController.startSession() and display the live camera  preview. While a session is active, a stop button shall be visible;  tapping it shall call AutoBoksController.stopSession() and hide the  camera preview. If permission is denied during startSession(), the button  shall revert to its inactive state and present an error message.  The button shall be absent when AutoBoks is unavailable or unconfigured.</td></tr>
<tr><td>REQ_CV_MODEL_LIFECYCLE</td><td>REQ-CV-001</td><td>ModelService shall correctly track the ModelInstallState machine:  notInstalled → downloading (on startDownload) → installed (on  downloadComplete) or back to notInstalled (on cancelledOrFailed).  download() shall reject a downloaded file whose first 5 bytes begin  with "&lt;" (HTML guard) and transition to cancelledOrFailed.  VisionService.isAvailable() shall return false when ModelService  reports notInstalled, and true when installed.  identifyItem() shall throw a descriptive exception if the output  tensor is all-zero.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</body></html>